<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31315" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noxĭōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		noxia (postAug.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Very hurtful, injurious</i>, or <i>noxious</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 7, 10, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noxiosissimo animali (al. noxissimo s.
					noxiissimo),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Clem. 1, 26, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Full of guilt, vicious, sinful</i>: animi perditi
			noxiosique, v. l. <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 70, 23</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noxiosissimum corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 130, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
